comments[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T21:01:07.495Z",codex-searxng-agent,"Orientation evidence: all 53 prior items and 527 valid history entries were inspected across every status. There are no open or in-progress items and no duplicate candidate for this operational delta."
  "2026-07-24T21:06:25.141Z",codex-searxng-agent,"Implementation checkpoint: added explicit autocomplete and read-only instance stats/errors commands; TOON is the default agent format and JSON is available for jq/CI. Updated both live E2E and release gates so the actual installed searxng binary must exercise these surfaces."
  "2026-07-24T21:18:38.334Z",codex-searxng-agent,"Pre-commit acceptance: 20 files and 938 tests pass at exact 100% statements/branches/functions/lines; TypeScript, ESLint, Prettier, 20/20 module docstrings, jscpd, ShellCheck, Bun audit, Trivy high/critical/secret/misconfiguration scan, history secret scan, generated changelog checks, npm/Bun package smoke, isolated installed-command help matrix, and governed LAN live E2E are green."
notes[2]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T21:01:07.495Z",codex-searxng-agent,"Preserve JSON-first search with HTML fallback because this governed instance intentionally returns 403 for format=json while HTML search is enabled. Do not regress the existing TOON v4, global-state, or unlimited-cache contracts."
  "2026-07-24T21:06:26.363Z",codex-searxng-agent,Operational stats deliberately compose the stable /config JSON and /stats/errors JSON contracts. The browser-oriented /stats and /preferences HTML pages remain discoverable through instance capability metadata but are not scraped into a brittle private schema.
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-24T21:01:07.495Z",codex-searxng-agent,"Current upstream and live service expose configuration, autocomplete, preferences, statistics, and error metrics in addition to search; raw search params already cover the user-facing query surface, while operational metrics remain the meaningful CLI parity gap."
